  "text": "Recipe: Stuffed Tofu Tikki\nCreator: Mrs N K Manku\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: jowar (sorghum) flour, kala chana (brown chickpeas), vegetables of your choice (grated or minced), grated plantain, corn, medium sized onion (minced), boiled mashed potato, soy milk residue, peanut yogurt, green beans, grated carrot, amla pieces, raisins, flaxseed powder, grated ginger, green chili, raw mango powder, turmeric powder, black pepper, hing (asafoetida), cumin seeds, carom seeds, mustard powder, garlic powder, tofu slices, sesame seeds\nCooking methods: no-cook, bake\nInstructions: Mix all the ingredients into a firm dough. Add some more flour if required. Make balls with the dough. Stuff them with tofu slices. Flatten them into the shape of tikkis. Sprinkle some sesame seeds. Bake both sides for 30 and 10 minutes, respectively, at 180 C\nNotes: A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (sorghum flour), BEANS (kala chana, tofu), TUBERS (potato), RAINBOW VEGGIES (onion, green beans, carrot), FRUIT & BERRIES (plantain, amla pieces) NUTS & SEEDS (peanut yogurt, flaxseed powder, sesame seeds), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
